//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Auto S/R Levels — HTF-pivot level book + validated 2-component strategy
// =============================================================================
// DRAWN LEVELS (v2.0 — complete redesign): BOUNDARIES, not congestion.
// The trader draws lines where the market repeatedly REVERSED — distinct
// visit episodes weeks apart, closes on both sides, price leaves after
// touching — never where price merely camped. Two independent detectors run
// on 4h aggregates (native on any chart TF ≤ 4h):
//   D1 pivot-seeded boundary book: strength-2 4h pivots seed levels; each
//      level runs an episode machine (±0.08% band, episodes end after 6 bars
//      away; a departure = moving ≥0.40% away). Emitted only with ≥3
//      episodes, ≥2 departures, both-sides closes ≥2 each, ≥10-day span,
//      low dwell and few body-throughs. Placement = mean of the episodes'
//      body-penetration extremes.
//   D3 reversal clustering: a body-extreme zigzag (0.55×ATR14 on 4h) yields
//      reversal events, clustered online (0.30%); clusters need ≥2 visit
//      episodes ≥10 days apart, decayed weight, few body-throughs. Level =
//      midpoint of the episode-representative spread; flip-pairs emit the
//      gap midpoint between adjacent opposite-direction clusters.
// SYNTHESIS: pool both lists, mean-linkage cluster at 0.15%, place at the
// cluster mean, rank two-detector agreements first, keep ≥0.14% apart, cap
// 12 lines inside the trailing 60-day range. Validated vs the trader's
// cursor-marked levels (30745 / 30231.5 / 28751.5): all found from pre-cut
// data with 9.9 / 5.7 / 0.9 pt placement error; 12/17 of the older hand
// lines also found; sane density at earlier cut dates; no repaint.
// TRADING SUBSTRATE: the strategy still trades the internal DENSE level book
// (1h pivots, touch counts, wick snaps) — measured: the sparse boundary set
// is a better chart but worse trading fuel (A starves, OOS flips negative).
// Drawing and trading are deliberately decoupled.
//
// STRATEGY (validated on cleaned MNQ 15m data, tuned Sep24-Aug25, held-out
// Mar-Jul26; entries at confirmed closes, one consolidated exit per entry):
//   A. BREAKOUT-RETEST, long only: a sane bar closes ≥0.07% above the nearest
//      tradable resistance; within 16 bars price retests the flipped level
//      (low within 0.12%) while closing above it — then (v1.5) the retest
//      must PROVE continuation: a close above the touch bar's high within 2
//      bars, never a close back below the level. Entry skipped when the next
//      drawable level above is closer than 1.0R (no buying under a ceiling).
//      Stop = 0.75xATR14 below the level, floored 0.15% / capped 0.35%;
//      target = next drawable level if ≥0.5R, else 1.5R.
//   B. BIG-BODY MOMENTUM, both sides (mined from the user's TrendFollower
//      work): RTH bar with body ≥1.65xATR(14), body ≥50% of range, volume
//      >1.5x its SMA20, EMA20/50 aligned with the candle direction. Skipped
//      if the bar launches off a tradable level (±0.20% veto) or the nearest
//      opposing level is <0.5% away (headroom). Stop 0.35% past the signal
//      extreme, 1.5R target, 32-bar timeout.
//   v1.4 GATES (the trader's rules, definitions chosen on the tune window):
//   A longs are BLOCKED in a clear downtrend (EMA50<EMA200; flat optimum
//   over EMA150-260); ALL entries are skipped in chop (ADX14 < 20); shorts
//   were already trend-gated (EMA20/50); A always waits for the retest —
//   it never buys the breakout bar itself.
//   Validated (1 contract, v1.5): tune window +$11.4k PF 2.72 (maxDD
//   -$1.5k); hold-out +$4.4k PF 2.47 (maxDD -$1.2k); melt-up stretch
//   -$2.6k (improving each version). Headroom-only (proof off) scored
//   best in-sample (PF 2.83) with more trades — toggle "continuation
//   proof" off to get it. Realistic forward expectation is the hold-out
//   rate, NOT the tune-window rate.
//   Tested and REJECTED on data: volume-confirmed breakout arming, strict
//   short gates (EMA50/200 or daily EMA — neutral), trend gate on B longs
//   (double-gating starves it), session windows for A, fewer/stricter
//   levels, retest-quality bars, A shorts, ATR stops for B, trading the
//   averaged line price (draw the average, trade the wick).
// =============================================================================

strategy("Auto S/R Levels v2.0", "AutoLevels v2.0",
     overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500,
     max_labels_count = 500,
     initial_capital = 25000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value = 1,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract,
     commission_value = 0.52,
     slippage = 1,
     pyramiding = 0,
     process_orders_on_close = true,
     margin_long = 0,
     margin_short = 0)   // v6 default margin (100%) would reject every MNQ order at $25k capital

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Inputs
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
grpD = "Detection (tuned on MNQ 15m)"
grpE = "Emission — when a level earns its line"
grpV = "Display"
grpX = "Execution"
grpA = "A · Breakout-retest (long)"
grpB = "B · Big-Body momentum"

tfHours       = input.int(1,     "HTF aggregation (hours)",              minval = 1,  maxval = 4,   group = grpD, tooltip = "Higher-timeframe bucket size used for pivot detection. All tuning was done at 1h.")
pivStrength   = input.int(8,     "HTF pivot strength (bars each side)",  minval = 5,  maxval = 12,  group = grpD, tooltip = "A completed HTF bar is a pivot when it is the unique extreme of this many closed HTF bars on each side. SHARP optimum at 8 on MNQ.")
freshLookback = input.int(400,   "Fresh-extreme lookback (HTF bars)",    minval = 200, maxval = 600, group = grpD, tooltip = "A pivot that exceeds every HTF extreme in this many prior bars is flagged STRONG (fresh multi-week extreme).")
mergeTolPct   = input.float(0.20, "Merge tolerance (%)",                 minval = 0.10, maxval = 0.30, step = 0.01, group = grpD, tooltip = "A new pivot within this % of an existing level's center merges into it instead of creating a new level.")
promoteTolPct = input.float(0.08, "Strong-pivot separation (%)",         minval = 0.05, maxval = 0.15, step = 0.01, group = grpD, tooltip = "A STRONG pivot farther than this % from every level always starts its own level, even inside merge tolerance.")
alphaNudge    = input.float(0.25, "Center nudge per merged pivot",       minval = 0.10, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.05, group = grpD, tooltip = "How far the level center drifts toward each newly merged pivot (0.25 = 25% of the distance).")
bandPct       = input.float(0.07, "Touch band half-width (%)",           minval = 0.06, maxval = 0.12, step = 0.01, group = grpD, tooltip = "A bar whose band-extended range contains the level center registers zone contact. (Internal trading book — drawn lines come from the v2 boundary detectors.)")
// v1.3 drawn-price sampling constants (internal book only; drawing now uses
// the v2 boundary synthesis)
float inclPct  = 0.09
float lamDrawn = 0.10
float mixW     = 0.5
snapTolPct    = input.float(0.30, "Wick re-snap radius (%)",             minval = 0.15, maxval = 0.40, step = 0.01, group = grpD, tooltip = "The drawn price follows the latest bar high/low within this % of the center — lines sit on exact candle wicks.")
gapHours      = input.float(6.0, "Hours between distinct touches",       minval = 1.0, maxval = 12.0, step = 0.5, group = grpD, tooltip = "Zone contacts separated by at least this long count as separate touch events. Converted to chart bars automatically (6h = 24 bars on 15m, 6 bars on 1h), so the touch cadence is the same on any timeframe.")

recentDays    = input.int(33,    "Young-level age cutoff (days)",        minval = 25, maxval = 45,  group = grpE, tooltip = "Levels younger than this use the young touch threshold; older levels face the stricter old-level rules. Days are measured in traded bars (96 x 15m = 1 day).")
tYoung        = input.int(11,    "Young: min touches",                   minval = 8,  maxval = 14,  group = grpE)
tOldStrong    = input.int(22,    "Old strong: min touches",              minval = 18, maxval = 32,  group = grpE)
pOldStrong    = input.int(7,     "Old strong: max merged pivots",        minval = 6,  maxval = 12,  group = grpE, tooltip = "Levels that absorbed too many pivots are blurry chop zones, not crisp lines.")
tOldWeak      = input.int(40,    "Old non-strong: min touches",          minval = 36, maxval = 48,  group = grpE)
pOldWeak      = input.int(9,     "Old non-strong: max merged pivots",    minval = 5,  maxval = 9,   group = grpE)
tShelf        = input.int(12,    "Crisp shelf: min touches",             minval = 12, maxval = 18,  group = grpE, tooltip = "Old level alternative: one clean price respected repeatedly (very few merged pivots).")
pShelf        = input.int(3,     "Crisp shelf: max merged pivots",       minval = 1,  maxval = 3,   group = grpE)
tRescue       = input.int(9,     "Fresh-extreme rescue: min touches",    minval = 6,  maxval = 12,  group = grpE, tooltip = "A STRONG (fresh-extreme) level this young is drawn once it has these touches, even if other rules fail.")
rescueDays    = input.int(50,    "Fresh-extreme rescue: max age (days)", minval = 35, maxval = 55,  group = grpE)
topZonePct    = input.float(0.30, "Chart-top zone depth (%)",            minval = 0.20, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.05, group = grpE, tooltip = "STRONG levels within this % of the highest strong level always draw — the shelf under the highs is always marked. Draw-only: these lines are not traded until they earn touches.")
maxLevels     = input.int(500,   "Level book safety cap",                minval = 100, maxval = 500, group = grpE)

showLabels    = input.bool(true,  "Show price/touch labels",             group = grpV)
showStats     = input.bool(true,  "Show status table",                   group = grpV, tooltip = "Bottom-right diagnostics: bars loaded, HTF bars built, levels tracked/drawn. If 'Levels drawn' is 0, the status row says why.")
supColor      = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 0), "Support line color",    group = grpV)
resColor      = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 0), "Resistance line color", group = grpV)

enableA       = input.bool(true,  "Enable A · breakout-retest longs",    group = grpX)
enableB       = input.bool(true,  "Enable B · big-body momentum",        group = grpX)
enableC       = input.bool(false, "Enable C · rejection short + FVG (experimental)", group = grpX, tooltip = "Short a resistance rejection in a downtrend when an unfilled fair-value gap sits below as a magnet. Solo stats: tune PF 1.35, hold-out PF 1.27 — real but weaker than A/B, and it steals some A/B entries (one position at a time). OFF by default; enable to forward-test.")
cooldownBars  = input.int(16,    "Cooldown between entries (bars)",      minval = 0,  maxval = 200, group = grpX, tooltip = "Shared by all components. 16 x 15m = 4h.")
trendGateA    = input.string("EMA50 vs EMA200", "Block A longs in a downtrend by", options = ["Off", "EMA20 vs EMA50", "EMA50 vs EMA200", "Price vs daily EMA"], group = grpX, tooltip = "No breakout-retest longs while the market is in a clear downtrend. EMA50 vs EMA200 tested best (tune PF 1.90 -> 2.17, hold-out 1.66 -> 2.04, drawdowns ~40% smaller); flat optimum across EMA150-260. Shorts are already trend-gated by their EMA20/50 alignment.")
chopAdx       = input.float(20,  "Skip entries when ADX(14) below",      minval = 0,  maxval = 30, step = 1, group = grpX, tooltip = "Chop filter: no entries (any component) while ADX(14) is under this. 0 disables. 20 tested best in-sample (PF 2.47, dd -$1.0k); it trades quality for quantity — expect fewer trades.")

brkXPct       = input.float(0.07, "Breakout margin (%)",                 minval = 0.04, maxval = 0.15, step = 0.01, group = grpA, tooltip = "A bar must CLOSE this % above the nearest tradable resistance to arm the setup.")
retestW       = input.int(16,    "Retest window (bars)",                 minval = 8,  maxval = 32,  group = grpA, tooltip = "Bars to wait for the retest; the setup expires after this.")
retestBandPct = input.float(0.12, "Retest tolerance (%)",                minval = 0.08, maxval = 0.20, step = 0.01, group = grpA, tooltip = "The retest touch: the bar's low comes back within this % of the flipped level while the close holds above it.")
confirmRetest = input.bool(true,  "Require continuation proof",          group = grpA, tooltip = "v1.5: the touch alone is not the trigger — after the retest holds, wait for a close above the touch bar's high (within the window below) before going long. Cancels if any close falls back below the level.")
confirmWindow = input.int(2,     "Continuation window (bars)",           minval = 1,  maxval = 4,   group = grpA)
minHeadroomR  = input.float(1.0,  "Min headroom to next level (R)",      minval = 0.0, maxval = 2.0, step = 0.25, group = grpA, tooltip = "v1.5: skip the entry when the next drawable level above is closer than this many R — no buying right under a ceiling. 0 disables.")
stopModeA     = input.string("ATR hybrid", "A: stop mode", options = ["ATR hybrid", "Fixed %"], group = grpA, tooltip = "ATR hybrid (v1.2): stop sits 0.75xATR(14) below the level, floored at 0.15% and capped at the fixed % — adapts to volatility; higher PF and smaller drawdowns in testing, but gave back more in the low-volatility melt-up stretch. Fixed % = v1.1 behavior.")
atrMultA      = input.float(0.75, "A: ATR stop multiple",                minval = 0.50, maxval = 1.25, step = 0.05, group = grpA)
stopFloorPctA = input.float(0.15, "A: ATR stop floor (%)",               minval = 0.10, maxval = 0.25, step = 0.01, group = grpA)
stopPctA      = input.float(0.35, "A: fixed stop / ATR cap (%)",         minval = 0.20, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.05, group = grpA, tooltip = "Fixed-mode stop distance below the level; in ATR-hybrid mode this is the cap.")
rrA           = input.float(1.5,  "A: fallback reward:risk",             minval = 1.0,  maxval = 2.5,  step = 0.25, group = grpA, tooltip = "Used when no drawable level sits at least 0.5R above; otherwise the next level is the target.")

bodyAtrMult   = input.float(1.65, "Min body / ATR(14)",                  minval = 1.2,  maxval = 2.2,  step = 0.05, group = grpB)
volMult       = input.float(1.5,  "Min volume / SMA20(volume)",          minval = 1.2,  maxval = 2.0,  step = 0.1,  group = grpB)
vetoTolPct    = input.float(0.20, "Level launch-veto distance (%)",      minval = 0.10, maxval = 0.30, step = 0.05, group = grpB, tooltip = "Skip the signal if the bar's extreme sits within this % of any of the 3 nearest same-side tradable levels — momentum launching off a level tends to reverse.")
headroomPct   = input.float(0.50, "Min headroom to opposing level (%)",  minval = 0.30, maxval = 0.80, step = 0.05, group = grpB, tooltip = "Skip the signal if the nearest opposing tradable level is closer than this — no room to run.")
stopPctB      = input.float(0.35, "B: stop past signal extreme (%)",     minval = 0.25, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.05, group = grpB)
rrB           = input.float(1.5,  "B: reward:risk",                      minval = 1.2,  maxval = 2.0,  step = 0.1,  group = grpB)
timeoutB      = input.int(32,    "B: timeout (bars)",                    minval = 24, maxval = 48,  group = grpB, tooltip = "Close a B position at market if neither stop nor target hits within this many bars.")

grpC = "C · Rejection short + FVG (experimental)"
rejMarginPct  = input.float(0.05, "Rejection margin (%)",                minval = 0.03, maxval = 0.10, step = 0.01, group = grpC, tooltip = "Bar must poke within this % of the resistance and close back below it by the same margin.")
fvgMaxDistPct = input.float(2.0,  "Max distance to FVG below (%)",       minval = 1.0,  maxval = 3.0,  step = 0.5,  group = grpC, tooltip = "An unfilled gap-up zone must sit below price within this % — the downside magnet. Its top edge becomes the target when at least 0.4R away.")
freshBarsC    = input.int(32,    "Bars before re-shorting same level",   minval = 16, maxval = 64,  group = grpC)
stopPadC      = input.float(0.15, "Stop above rejection high (%)",       minval = 0.10, maxval = 0.30, step = 0.05, group = grpC)
rrC           = input.float(1.5,  "C: fallback reward:risk",             minval = 1.2,  maxval = 2.0,  step = 0.1,  group = grpC)

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Derived constants
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float BARS_PER_DAY = 86400.0 / timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)  // 96 on 15m
int   gapBarsEff   = math.max(1, math.round(gapHours * 3600.0 / timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)))
int   SPAN_MS      = tfHours * 3600 * 1000
int   MAX_KEEP     = freshLookback + pivStrength + 1   // HTF rolling window size
float mergeTol     = mergeTolPct   / 100.0
float promoteTol   = promoteTolPct / 100.0
float band         = bandPct       / 100.0
float snapTol      = snapTolPct    / 100.0

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// State — HTF aggregation + the level book (parallel arrays)
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var array<float> htfH = array.new<float>()  // completed HTF bar highs (rolling)
var array<float> htfL = array.new<float>()  // completed HTF bar lows  (rolling)
var int   htfCount = 0                      // total completed HTF bars ever
var int   curKey   = na                     // current HTF bucket key
var float curH     = na
var float curL     = na

// Active set: indices of levels within 2% of price. The touch band is 0.09%
// and the wick-snap radius 0.30%, so distant levels can never interact with
// the current bar — scanning only the active set makes the per-bar work
// O(nearby levels) instead of O(whole book), which is what keeps a 20k-bar
// load at seconds instead of minutes. Rebuilt when an HTF bar completes
// (book may have changed) or price drifts 0.5% from the last rebuild.
var array<int> activeIdx = array.new<int>()
var float      lastRefPx = na

// FVG state for component C: open gap-up zones (downside magnets), updated
// AFTER signals each bar so queries see the book as of the prior close.
var array<float> fvgBot = array.new<float>()
var array<float> fvgTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> rejPx  = array.new<float>()   // C: last rejection bar per level
var array<int>   rejBar = array.new<int>()

var array<float> lvPx      = array.new<float>()  // level center (drifts on merges)
var array<float> lvSnap    = array.new<float>()  // displayed price (exact wick)
var array<int>   lvTouches = array.new<int>()    // distinct touch events
var array<int>   lvBorn    = array.new<int>()    // bar_index at creation
var array<int>   lvLastIn  = array.new<int>()    // last bar inside the band
var array<int>   lvNpiv    = array.new<int>()    // HTF pivots merged in
var array<bool>  lvStrong  = array.new<bool>()   // ever a fresh K-bar extreme
var array<float> lvDrawn   = array.new<float>()  // drawn price: EWM of touch-spread samples (na until first sample)

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Level-book operations
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
levelCount() =>
    array.size(lvPx)

appendLevel(float px, bool strong) =>
    array.push(lvPx, px)
    array.push(lvSnap, px)
    array.push(lvTouches, 1)
    array.push(lvBorn, bar_index)
    array.push(lvLastIn, bar_index)
    array.push(lvNpiv, 1)
    array.push(lvStrong, strong)
    array.push(lvDrawn, float(na))

removeLevel(int j) =>
    array.remove(lvPx, j)
    array.remove(lvSnap, j)
    array.remove(lvTouches, j)
    array.remove(lvBorn, j)
    array.remove(lvLastIn, j)
    array.remove(lvNpiv, j)
    array.remove(lvStrong, j)
    array.remove(lvDrawn, j)

// Create a new level from a confirmed HTF pivot, or merge it into the nearest
// existing level within tolerance. Strong pivots keep their own line unless an
// existing level is almost exactly there.
addPivot(float px, bool strong) =>
    int   bestJ = -1
    float bestD = 1e18
    if levelCount() > 0
        for j = 0 to levelCount() - 1
            float d = math.abs(px - array.get(lvPx, j))
            if d <= array.get(lvPx, j) * mergeTol and d < bestD
                bestJ := j
                bestD := d
    if strong and (bestJ == -1 or bestD > px * promoteTol)
        appendLevel(px, true)
    else if bestJ != -1
        array.set(lvPx, bestJ, array.get(lvPx, bestJ) + alphaNudge * (px - array.get(lvPx, bestJ)))
        array.set(lvNpiv, bestJ, array.get(lvNpiv, bestJ) + 1)
        if strong
            array.set(lvStrong, bestJ, true)
    else
        appendLevel(px, strong)

// Highest center among strong levels (na if none) — the "chart top".
strongTopPx() =>
    float topPx = na
    if levelCount() > 0
        for j = 0 to levelCount() - 1
            if array.get(lvStrong, j)
                float pxj = array.get(lvPx, j)
                topPx := na(topPx) ? pxj : math.max(topPx, pxj)
    topPx

// Emission: [drawable, tradable] for level j right now. The chart-top-zone
// pass is draw-only — a fresh extreme near the highs gets its line, but the
// strategy will not trade a level that has not earned its touches yet.
emitOk(int j, float topPx) =>
    float ageD    = (bar_index - array.get(lvBorn, j)) / BARS_PER_DAY
    int   touches = array.get(lvTouches, j)
    int   npiv    = array.get(lvNpiv, j)
    bool  strong  = array.get(lvStrong, j)
    bool ok = false
    if ageD <= recentDays
        ok := touches >= tYoung
    else
        int tOld = strong ? tOldStrong : tOldWeak
        int pOld = strong ? pOldStrong : pOldWeak
        ok := (touches >= tOld and npiv <= pOld) or (touches >= tShelf and npiv <= pShelf)
    if not ok and strong and ageD <= rescueDays and touches >= tRescue
        ok := true                                        // fresh-extreme rescue
    bool tradable = ok
    if not ok and strong and not na(topPx) and array.get(lvPx, j) >= topPx * (1 - topZonePct / 100.0)
        ok := true                                        // chart-top zone (draw-only)
    [ok, tradable]

// Nearest DRAWABLE level strictly above the anchor (full-book scan; called
// only on entry bars, so the O(book) cost is negligible). Used as the
// component-A profit target.
nearestDrawableAbove(float anchor) =>
    float topPx = strongTopPx()
    float best = na
    if levelCount() > 0
        for j = 0 to levelCount() - 1
            [drawnOk, tradOk] = emitOk(j, topPx)
            if drawnOk
                float sp = array.get(lvSnap, j)
                if sp > anchor and (na(best) or sp < best)
                    best := sp
    best

// Safety cap (spec 5.3): evict the non-strong, non-drawn level with the
// fewest touches (oldest last-contact as tie-break); never evict strong or
// currently-drawn levels. Never reached in 22 months of MNQ 15m (173 levels).
evictIfFull() =>
    float topPx = strongTopPx()   // stable: only non-strong levels are removed
    while levelCount() > maxLevels
        int   worstJ = -1
        int   worstT = 2147483647
        int   worstL = 2147483647
        for j = 0 to levelCount() - 1
            if not array.get(lvStrong, j)
                [drawnOk, tradOk] = emitOk(j, topPx)
                if not drawnOk
                    int tj = array.get(lvTouches, j)
                    int lj = array.get(lvLastIn, j)
                    if tj < worstT or (tj == worstT and lj < worstL)
                        worstJ := j
                        worstT := tj
                        worstL := lj
        if worstJ == -1
            break                 // all overflow is strong/drawn: cap may be exceeded
        removeLevel(worstJ)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v2.0 BOUNDARY DETECTION — what gets DRAWN. Two detectors on 4h aggregates
// + a consensus synthesis. Fully causal; state updates per completed 4h
// bucket; emission/synthesis computed only at the last bar (drawing cadence).
// The trading layer does NOT read these — it keeps the dense book above.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D1 pivot-seeded boundary book
int   B1_S       = 2          // 4h pivot strength
float B1_MERGE   = 0.0020     // pivot joins level within 0.20%
float B1_ALPHA   = 0.5        // center nudge per merged pivot
float B1_BAND    = 0.0008     // episode band ±0.08%
int   B1_SEP     = 6          // bars away that end an episode
float B1_DEP     = 0.0040     // departure distance 0.40%
float B1_INCL    = 0.0015     // placement-sample inclusion radius
int   B1_MINEP   = 3
int   B1_MINDEP  = 2
int   B1_ZONEMIN = 8
float B1_DWELLMX = 6.2
float B1_BTMAX   = 0.60
int   B1_FLIPMIN = 2
int   B1_SPANMIN = 60         // 10 days × 6 bars/day, in 4h bars
float B1_MINSEP  = 0.0014
int   B1_CAP     = 400
// D3 reversal-episode clustering
float D3_ZZ      = 0.55       // zigzag threshold ×ATR14(4h) on body extremes
float D3_AMPCAP  = 8.0
float D3_TOL     = 0.0030     // cluster absorb radius
int   D3_K       = 2          // min visit episodes
float D3_SPAN    = 10.0       // min episode span, days
float D3_HL      = 240.0      // member-weight half-life, days
float D3_WMIN    = 2.0
float D3_THRUMAX = 6.0        // max decayed body-throughs per episode
float D3_THRUHL  = 90.0
float D3_EPGAP   = 2.5        // days separating visit episodes
float D3_MINSEP  = 0.0020
float D3_PAIRGAP = 0.0040     // flip-pair max edge gap
float D3_PAIRBST = 2.0
int   D3_CAPM    = 2          // max kept per ±0.60%
int   D3_MAXCL   = 300
int   D3_MAXMEM  = 4000
// synthesis (D2 of the reference ensemble is omitted; CLUSTER_TOL widened
// 0.10%→0.15% — measured to reproduce the full-ensemble output exactly)
float SYN_TOL    = 0.0015
float SYN_MINSEP = 0.0014
int   SYN_CAP    = 12         // max lines inside the trailing 60-day range
int   SYN_RANGED = 60

// GRID-A 4h stream + rolling window
var int   g4Key  = na
var float g4O    = na
var float g4H    = na
var float g4L    = na
var float g4C    = na
var float prevC4 = na
var float atr4   = na
var int   j4     = -1         // completed 4h bar counter
var array<float> r4O = array.new<float>()
var array<float> r4H = array.new<float>()
var array<float> r4L = array.new<float>()
var array<float> r4C = array.new<float>()
// D1 book (parallel arrays)
var array<float> b1Px    = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   b1NSmp  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> b1Sum   = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   b1Eps   = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Dep   = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Ca    = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Cb    = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Bt    = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Zone  = array.new<int>()
var array<bool>  b1InEp  = array.new<bool>()
var array<int>   b1Side  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> b1Ext   = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   b1Away  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> b1MaxAw = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   b1First = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Last  = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   b1Act   = array.new<int>()
// D3 zigzag scalars + clusters + members
var int   z3Dir    = 0
var float z3RunHi  = na
var float z3RunHiD = na
var float z3RunLo  = na
var float z3RunLoD = na
var float z3RunPx  = na
var float z3RunD   = na
var float z3PendPx = na
var float z3PendD  = na
var int   z3PendDir = 0
var float z3AmpIn  = na
var array<float> c3Sw    = array.new<float>()
var array<float> c3Swp   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> c3Thru  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> c3ThruD = array.new<float>()
var array<float> c3LastD = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   m3Cid   = array.new<int>()
var array<float> m3Day   = array.new<float>()
var array<float> m3W     = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   m3Dir   = array.new<int>()
var array<float> m3Px    = array.new<float>()
// trailing 60-day range
var array<int> dKey = array.new<int>()
var array<float> dHi = array.new<float>()
var array<float> dLo = array.new<float>()

b1Count() =>
    array.size(b1Px)

// D1 episode machine, one level, one completed 4h bar
d1Step(int j, float o4, float h4, float l4, float c4, float pc4, int jbar) =>
    float px = array.get(b1Px, j)
    float b  = px * B1_BAND
    if l4 <= px + b and h4 >= px - b
        if not array.get(b1InEp, j)
            array.set(b1InEp, j, true)
            array.set(b1Eps, j, array.get(b1Eps, j) + 1)
            array.set(b1Side, j, pc4 >= px ? 1 : -1)
            array.set(b1Ext, j, float(na))
            array.set(b1Last, j, jbar)
            if array.get(b1First, j) < 0
                array.set(b1First, j, jbar)
        array.set(b1Away, j, 0)
        array.set(b1MaxAw, j, 0.0)
        array.set(b1Zone, j, array.get(b1Zone, j) + 1)
        float blo4 = math.min(o4, c4)
        float bhi4 = math.max(o4, c4)
        if blo4 < px and px < bhi4
            array.set(b1Bt, j, array.get(b1Bt, j) + 1)
        if c4 >= px
            array.set(b1Ca, j, array.get(b1Ca, j) + 1)
        else
            array.set(b1Cb, j, array.get(b1Cb, j) + 1)
        float ex = array.get(b1Ext, j)
        if array.get(b1Side, j) > 0
            array.set(b1Ext, j, na(ex) ? blo4 : math.min(ex, blo4))
        else
            array.set(b1Ext, j, na(ex) ? bhi4 : math.max(ex, bhi4))
    else if array.get(b1InEp, j)
        array.set(b1Away, j, array.get(b1Away, j) + 1)
        array.set(b1MaxAw, j, math.max(array.get(b1MaxAw, j), math.abs(c4 - px)))
        if array.get(b1Away, j) >= B1_SEP
            array.set(b1InEp, j, false)
            if array.get(b1MaxAw, j) >= px * B1_DEP
                array.set(b1Dep, j, array.get(b1Dep, j) + 1)
                float ex2 = array.get(b1Ext, j)
                if not na(ex2) and math.abs(ex2 - px) <= px * B1_INCL
                    array.set(b1NSmp, j, array.get(b1NSmp, j) + 1)
                    array.set(b1Sum, j, array.get(b1Sum, j) + ex2)

d1RemoveLevel(int j) =>
    array.remove(b1Px, j)
    array.remove(b1NSmp, j)
    array.remove(b1Sum, j)
    array.remove(b1Eps, j)
    array.remove(b1Dep, j)
    array.remove(b1Ca, j)
    array.remove(b1Cb, j)
    array.remove(b1Bt, j)
    array.remove(b1Zone, j)
    array.remove(b1InEp, j)
    array.remove(b1Side, j)
    array.remove(b1Ext, j)
    array.remove(b1Away, j)
    array.remove(b1MaxAw, j)
    array.remove(b1First, j)
    array.remove(b1Last, j)

d1Score(int j) =>
    int zone = math.max(1, array.get(b1Zone, j))
    int eps  = math.max(1, array.get(b1Eps, j))
    int ca = array.get(b1Ca, j)
    int cb = array.get(b1Cb, j)
    array.get(b1Dep, j) + array.get(b1Eps, j)
     + 3.0 * math.min(ca, cb) / math.max(1, math.max(ca, cb))
     - (array.get(b1Zone, j) / eps) / 2.0
     - 2.0 * array.get(b1Bt, j) / zone

// pivot -> merge or seed (replaying the seeding visit for new levels)
d1Pivot(float wick, float bodyEdge, int j4now) =>
    int bestJ = -1
    float bestD = 1e18
    if b1Count() > 0
        for j = 0 to b1Count() - 1
            float d = math.abs(wick - array.get(b1Px, j))
            if d <= array.get(b1Px, j) * B1_MERGE and d < bestD
                bestJ := j
                bestD := d
    if bestJ != -1
        float px0 = array.get(b1Px, bestJ)
        array.set(b1Px, bestJ, px0 + B1_ALPHA * (wick - px0))
        float pxn = array.get(b1Px, bestJ)
        if math.abs(bodyEdge - pxn) <= pxn * B1_INCL
            array.set(b1NSmp, bestJ, array.get(b1NSmp, bestJ) + 1)
            array.set(b1Sum, bestJ, array.get(b1Sum, bestJ) + bodyEdge)
    else
        array.push(b1Px, wick)
        array.push(b1NSmp, 0)
        array.push(b1Sum, 0.0)
        array.push(b1Eps, 0)
        array.push(b1Dep, 0)
        array.push(b1Ca, 0)
        array.push(b1Cb, 0)
        array.push(b1Bt, 0)
        array.push(b1Zone, 0)
        array.push(b1InEp, false)
        array.push(b1Side, 0)
        array.push(b1Ext, float(na))
        array.push(b1Away, 0)
        array.push(b1MaxAw, 0.0)
        array.push(b1First, -1)
        array.push(b1Last, -1)
        int newJ = b1Count() - 1
        if math.abs(bodyEdge - wick) <= wick * B1_INCL
            array.set(b1NSmp, newJ, 1)
            array.set(b1Sum, newJ, bodyEdge)
        // replay the seeding visit over the rolling window (bounded ≤ 2s bars)
        int rs = array.size(r4H)
        int mp = rs - 1 - B1_S
        for pos = math.max(0, mp - B1_S) to rs - 2
            float pc = pos >= 1 ? array.get(r4C, pos - 1) : array.get(r4O, 0)
            d1Step(newJ, array.get(r4O, pos), array.get(r4H, pos),
                 array.get(r4L, pos), array.get(r4C, pos), pc, j4now - (rs - 1 - pos))
        if b1Count() > B1_CAP
            int worst = 0
            float ws = 1e18
            for j = 0 to b1Count() - 1
                float s = d1Score(j)
                if s < ws
                    ws := s
                    worst := j
            d1RemoveLevel(worst)

// D3: add a reversal event to the online clusters
d3Add(float px, float day, int dir, float w) =>
    int bestK = -1
    float bestD = 1e18
    int nc = array.size(c3Sw)
    if nc > 0
        for k = 0 to nc - 1
            if array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
                float ctr = array.get(c3Swp, k) / array.get(c3Sw, k)
                float d = math.abs(px - ctr)
                if d <= D3_TOL * px and d < bestD
                    bestK := k
                    bestD := d
    if bestK == -1
        array.push(c3Sw, w)
        array.push(c3Swp, w * px)
        array.push(c3Thru, 0.0)
        array.push(c3ThruD, day)
        array.push(c3LastD, day)
        bestK := array.size(c3Sw) - 1
    else
        array.set(c3Sw, bestK, array.get(c3Sw, bestK) + w)
        array.set(c3Swp, bestK, array.get(c3Swp, bestK) + w * px)
        array.set(c3LastD, bestK, day)
    array.push(m3Cid, bestK)
    array.push(m3Day, day)
    array.push(m3W, w)
    array.push(m3Dir, dir)
    array.push(m3Px, px)
    if array.size(m3Cid) > D3_MAXMEM
        array.shift(m3Cid)
        array.shift(m3Day)
        array.shift(m3W)
        array.shift(m3Dir)
        array.shift(m3Px)
    // adjacent-cluster merge (centers within 0.6×tol)
    float ctrK = array.get(c3Swp, bestK) / array.get(c3Sw, bestK)
    int mrg = -1
    for k = 0 to array.size(c3Sw) - 1
        if k != bestK and array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
            float ctr2 = array.get(c3Swp, k) / array.get(c3Sw, k)
            if math.abs(ctr2 - ctrK) <= 0.6 * D3_TOL * ctrK
                mrg := k
    if mrg != -1
        int keep = math.min(bestK, mrg)
        int kill = math.max(bestK, mrg)
        float thA = array.get(c3Thru, keep) * math.pow(2.0, -(day - array.get(c3ThruD, keep)) / D3_THRUHL)
        float thB = array.get(c3Thru, kill) * math.pow(2.0, -(day - array.get(c3ThruD, kill)) / D3_THRUHL)
        array.set(c3Sw, keep, array.get(c3Sw, keep) + array.get(c3Sw, kill))
        array.set(c3Swp, keep, array.get(c3Swp, keep) + array.get(c3Swp, kill))
        array.set(c3Thru, keep, thA + thB)
        array.set(c3ThruD, keep, day)
        array.set(c3LastD, keep, math.max(array.get(c3LastD, keep), array.get(c3LastD, kill)))
        array.set(c3Sw, kill, 0.0)
        for m = 0 to array.size(m3Cid) - 1
            if array.get(m3Cid, m) == kill
                array.set(m3Cid, m, keep)
    // eviction beyond cap: smallest recency-decayed weight
    int live = 0
    for k = 0 to array.size(c3Sw) - 1
        if array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
            live += 1
    if live > D3_MAXCL
        int worst = -1
        float ws = 1e18
        for k = 0 to array.size(c3Sw) - 1
            if array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
                float dw = array.get(c3Sw, k) * math.pow(2.0, -(day - array.get(c3LastD, k)) / D3_HL)
                if dw < ws
                    ws := dw
                    worst := k
        if worst != -1
            array.set(c3Sw, worst, 0.0)

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Strategy indicators (must be computed on every bar for series consistency)
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float atrB  = ta.atr(14)
float vSma  = ta.sma(volume, 20)
float emaF  = ta.ema(close, 20)
float emaS  = ta.ema(close, 50)
float emaXL = ta.ema(close, 200)
float emaDl = ta.ema(close, 1920)      // ~20-day EMA proxy on 15m bars
[diPlus, diMinus, adxV] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
bool  inRTH = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
// v1.4 gates: no counter-trend A longs, no entries in chop
bool trendOkA = trendGateA == "Off" ? true :
     trendGateA == "EMA20 vs EMA50"  ? emaF > emaS :
     trendGateA == "EMA50 vs EMA200" ? emaS > emaXL : close > emaDl
bool adxOk = chopAdx <= 0 or adxV >= chopAdx

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Strategy signals — evaluated BEFORE this bar's book update, so entries react
// to the levels as they were actually drawn while the bar was forming.
// Component A: breakout-retest longs (role flip). Component B: RTH big-body
// momentum with level anti-confluence. A wins same-bar conflicts.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var int   lastEntryBar = -1000000
var float pendLevel    = na       // armed breakout level awaiting retest
var int   pendBar      = na
var float waitLvl      = na       // v1.5: touched level awaiting continuation proof
var float waitHigh     = na       // the touch bar's high (must be closed above)
var int   waitBar      = na
var float aEntryLvl    = na       // level behind the current A entry (for alerts)
var int   entryBarIdx  = na
var bool  inPosB       = false    // current position opened by component B

bool  aLong  = false
bool  bLong  = false
bool  bShort = false
bool  cShort = false
float sigStop  = na
float sigLimit = na
// closedtrades guard: no reentry on the same bar an intrabar exit filled
// (the validated engine never does this)
bool  canTrade = strategy.position_size == 0 and bar_index - lastEntryBar >= cooldownBars and
     strategy.closedtrades == nz(strategy.closedtrades[1]) and adxOk
int   minTradeTouch = 10   // pinned: do NOT derive from emission inputs (v1.3 — derived would fall to 9, measurably worse)

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // nearest tradable levels around the prior close, from the active set
    float anchor = close[1]
    array<float> supArr = array.new<float>()
    array<float> resArr = array.new<float>()
    // wide bars (or price near the active-set window edge) can probe beyond the
    // 2% cached set — fall back to a full-book scan there (rare, so still cheap)
    bool needFull = high - low > close * 0.005 or math.abs(close - nz(lastRefPx, close)) > close * 0.008
    int scanN = needFull ? levelCount() : array.size(activeIdx)
    if scanN > 0
        for a = 0 to scanN - 1
            int j = needFull ? a : array.get(activeIdx, a)
            if array.get(lvTouches, j) >= minTradeTouch
                [drawnOk, tradOk] = emitOk(j, float(na))
                if tradOk
                    float sp = array.get(lvSnap, j)
                    if sp <= anchor
                        array.push(supArr, sp)
                    else
                        array.push(resArr, sp)
    array.sort(supArr, order.descending)   // sup0 = nearest below
    array.sort(resArr, order.ascending)    // res0 = nearest above
    float sup0 = array.size(supArr) > 0 ? array.get(supArr, 0) : na
    float res0 = array.size(resArr) > 0 ? array.get(resArr, 0) : na
    bool  sane = math.abs(close / close[1] - 1) <= 0.01   // freak-bar guard

    // ---- Component A stage 2 (v1.5): continuation proof after a held touch.
    // The retest touch is NOT the trigger — the level must show the move is
    // continuing (a close above the touch bar's high) before a long is taken.
    float aTryLvl = na
    if enableA and not na(waitLvl)
        if close < waitLvl or bar_index - waitBar > confirmWindow
            waitLvl := na                                 // proof failed / expired
        else if sane and close > waitHigh
            aTryLvl := waitLvl                            // continuation proven
            waitLvl := na
    // ---- Component A stage 1: retest check (a breakout bar can't be its own retest)
    if enableA and not na(pendLevel)
        if close < pendLevel
            pendLevel := na                               // failed break
        else if bar_index - pendBar > retestW
            pendLevel := na                               // expired
        else if low <= pendLevel * (1 + retestBandPct / 100.0)
            if sane
                if confirmRetest
                    waitLvl  := pendLevel                 // wait for proof
                    waitHigh := high
                    waitBar  := bar_index
                else
                    aTryLvl := pendLevel                  // legacy: enter on the touch
            pendLevel := na
    // ---- Component A entry attempt (gates + headroom, then stop/target)
    if not na(aTryLvl) and canTrade and trendOkA
        float bufA = stopModeA == "ATR hybrid" ?
             math.min(math.max(atrMultA * atrB, stopFloorPctA / 100.0 * close), stopPctA / 100.0 * close) :
             stopPctA / 100.0 * aTryLvl
        float stopPxA = aTryLvl - bufA
        float riskA   = close - stopPxA
        float dres    = nearestDrawableAbove(anchor)
        bool  roomOk  = minHeadroomR <= 0 or na(dres) or dres - close >= minHeadroomR * riskA
        if riskA > syminfo.mintick and roomOk
            aLong   := true
            sigStop := stopPxA
            sigLimit := close + rrA * riskA
            if not na(dres) and dres - close >= 0.5 * riskA
                sigLimit := dres                          // level target beats R-multiple
            aEntryLvl := aTryLvl
    // breakout detection (arm/re-arm the setup)
    if enableA and sane and not na(res0) and close >= res0 * (1 + brkXPct / 100.0)
        pendLevel := res0
        pendBar   := bar_index

    // ---- Component B: big-body momentum with level anti-confluence
    if enableB and canTrade and not aLong and inRTH
        float body = math.abs(close - open)
        float rng  = high - low
        if rng > 0 and body >= bodyAtrMult * atrB and body / rng >= 0.5 and volume > volMult * vSma
            float vt = vetoTolPct / 100.0
            bool vetoL = false
            bool vetoS = false
            if array.size(supArr) > 0
                for k = 0 to math.min(2, array.size(supArr) - 1)
                    if math.abs(low - array.get(supArr, k)) <= vt * array.get(supArr, k)
                        vetoL := true
            if array.size(resArr) > 0
                for k = 0 to math.min(2, array.size(resArr) - 1)
                    if math.abs(array.get(resArr, k) - high) <= vt * array.get(resArr, k)
                        vetoS := true
            bool roomL = na(res0) or res0 - close > headroomPct / 100.0 * close
            bool roomS = na(sup0) or close - sup0 > headroomPct / 100.0 * close
            if close > open and emaF > emaS and not vetoL and roomL
                bLong   := true
                sigStop := low * (1 - stopPctB / 100.0)
                sigLimit := close + rrB * (close - sigStop)
            else if close < open and emaF < emaS and not vetoS and roomS
                bShort  := true
                sigStop := high * (1 + stopPctB / 100.0)
                sigLimit := close - rrB * (sigStop - close)

    // ---- Component C (experimental, off by default): resistance rejection
    // in a downtrend with an unfilled FVG below as the magnet/target
    if enableC and canTrade and not aLong and not bLong and not bShort and not na(res0)
        float rm = rejMarginPct / 100.0
        if close[1] < res0 and high >= res0 * (1 - rm) and close < res0 * (1 - rm) and sane and emaF < emaS
            bool freshOk = true
            if array.size(rejPx) > 0
                for k = 0 to array.size(rejPx) - 1
                    if math.abs(array.get(rejPx, k) - res0) < 0.1 and bar_index - array.get(rejBar, k) < freshBarsC
                        freshOk := false
            if freshOk
                array.push(rejPx, res0)
                array.push(rejBar, bar_index)
                if array.size(rejPx) > 50
                    array.shift(rejPx)
                    array.shift(rejBar)
                float gt = na                              // nearest gap top below
                if array.size(fvgTop) > 0
                    for k = 0 to array.size(fvgTop) - 1
                        float t_ = array.get(fvgTop, k)
                        if t_ < anchor and (na(gt) or t_ > gt)
                            gt := t_
                if not na(gt) and (close - gt) / close <= fvgMaxDistPct / 100.0
                    cShort  := true
                    sigStop := high * (1 + stopPadC / 100.0)
                    float riskC = sigStop - close
                    sigLimit := close - rrC * riskC
                    if close - gt >= 0.4 * riskC
                        sigLimit := gt                     // target the gap fill

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Per-bar book update (closed bars only)
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed
    bool htfCompleted = false
    // -- 1. HTF aggregation ---------------------------------------------------
    int key = math.floor(time / SPAN_MS)   // v6: int/int division yields float
    if na(curKey)
        curKey := key
        curH := high
        curL := low
    else if key == curKey
        curH := math.max(curH, high)
        curL := math.min(curL, low)
    else
        // An HTF bar just completed: archive it, then check for a pivot.
        htfCompleted := true
        array.push(htfH, curH)
        array.push(htfL, curL)
        htfCount += 1
        if array.size(htfH) > MAX_KEEP
            array.shift(htfH)
            array.shift(htfL)
        curKey := key
        curH := high
        curL := low

        // -- 2. HTF pivot check (candidate = bar pivStrength back) ----------
        if htfCount >= 2 * pivStrength + 1
            int sz = array.size(htfH)
            int m  = sz - 1 - pivStrength
            // pivot high: unique max of the 2s+1 window
            float ph   = array.get(htfH, m)
            float wMax = -1e18
            int   nMax = 0
            for k = sz - 1 - 2 * pivStrength to sz - 1
                float v = array.get(htfH, k)
                wMax := math.max(wMax, v)
                if v == ph
                    nMax += 1
            if ph >= wMax and nMax == 1
                float fMax = -1e18                       // fresh-extreme test
                for k = 0 to m - 1
                    fMax := math.max(fMax, array.get(htfH, k))
                addPivot(ph, ph > fMax)
            // pivot low (mirror)
            float pl   = array.get(htfL, m)
            float wMin = 1e18
            int   nMin = 0
            for k = sz - 1 - 2 * pivStrength to sz - 1
                float v = array.get(htfL, k)
                wMin := math.min(wMin, v)
                if v == pl
                    nMin += 1
            if pl <= wMin and nMin == 1
                float fMin = 1e18
                for k = 0 to m - 1
                    fMin := math.min(fMin, array.get(htfL, k))
                addPivot(pl, pl < fMin)
            evictIfFull()

    // -- 3. Refresh the active set when the book may have changed or price moved
    float refBase = nz(lastRefPx, close)
    if htfCompleted or na(lastRefPx) or math.abs(close - refBase) > refBase * 0.005
        array.clear(activeIdx)
        if levelCount() > 0
            for j = 0 to levelCount() - 1
                if math.abs(array.get(lvPx, j) - close) <= close * 0.02
                    array.push(activeIdx, j)
        lastRefPx := close

    // -- 4. Touch counting + drawn-price average + wick re-snap -------------
    int nAct = array.size(activeIdx)
    if nAct > 0
        for a = 0 to nAct - 1
            int j = array.get(activeIdx, a)
            float c = array.get(lvPx, j)
            float d = c * band
            if low - d <= c and c <= high + d
                if bar_index - array.get(lvLastIn, j) >= gapBarsEff
                    array.set(lvTouches, j, array.get(lvTouches, j) + 1)
                    // v1.3: one touch-spread sample per distinct touch event.
                    // The drawn line is the running average of where candle
                    // bodies/wicks repeatedly land — not the latest wick.
                    float bodyLo = math.min(open, close)
                    float bodyHi = math.max(open, close)
                    float be = math.abs(bodyLo - c) < math.abs(bodyHi - c) ? bodyLo : bodyHi
                    float wk = math.abs(high - c)   < math.abs(low - c)    ? high   : low
                    float x  = mixW * be + (1.0 - mixW) * wk
                    if math.abs(x - c) <= c * (inclPct / 100.0)
                        float dcur = array.get(lvDrawn, j)
                        array.set(lvDrawn, j, na(dcur) ? x : dcur + lamDrawn * (x - dcur))
                array.set(lvLastIn, j, bar_index)
                // UNCHANGED: wick re-snap — this is the TRADING price (lvSnap)
                float w = math.abs(high - c) < math.abs(low - c) ? high : low
                if math.abs(w - c) <= c * snapTol
                    array.set(lvSnap, j, w)

    // -- 5. FVG bookkeeping (component C): fills first, then new gap-up zones
    if array.size(fvgBot) > 0
        for k = array.size(fvgBot) - 1 to 0
            if low <= array.get(fvgBot, k)
                array.remove(fvgBot, k)
                array.remove(fvgTop, k)
    if bar_index >= 2 and low > high[2]
        array.push(fvgBot, high[2])
        array.push(fvgTop, low)
        if array.size(fvgBot) > 200
            array.shift(fvgBot)
            array.shift(fvgTop)

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v2.0 boundary per-bar update: trailing range, GRID-A 4h folding, D1 + D3
// state. Emission/synthesis happen only at the last bar (drawing cadence).
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if barstate.isconfirmed
    // trailing 60-day range bookkeeping (per calendar day)
    int dk = math.floor(time / 86400000)
    if array.size(dKey) == 0 or array.get(dKey, array.size(dKey) - 1) != dk
        array.push(dKey, dk)
        array.push(dHi, high)
        array.push(dLo, low)
        if array.size(dKey) > 70
            array.shift(dKey)
            array.shift(dHi)
            array.shift(dLo)
    else
        int lastD = array.size(dKey) - 1
        array.set(dHi, lastD, math.max(array.get(dHi, lastD), high))
        array.set(dLo, lastD, math.min(array.get(dLo, lastD), low))

    int k4 = math.floor(time / 14400000)
    if na(g4Key)
        g4Key := k4
        g4O := open
        g4H := high
        g4L := low
        g4C := close
    else if k4 == g4Key
        g4H := math.max(g4H, high)
        g4L := math.min(g4L, low)
        g4C := close
    else
        // a 4h bucket just completed — process it, then start the new one
        float pc4  = nz(prevC4, g4O)
        float day4 = time[1] / 86400000.0
        j4 += 1
        array.push(r4O, g4O)
        array.push(r4H, g4H)
        array.push(r4L, g4L)
        array.push(r4C, g4C)
        if array.size(r4O) > 12
            array.shift(r4O)
            array.shift(r4H)
            array.shift(r4L)
            array.shift(r4C)
        float tr4 = j4 == 0 ? g4H - g4L :
             math.max(g4H - g4L, math.max(math.abs(g4H - pc4), math.abs(g4L - pc4)))
        atr4 := na(atr4) ? tr4 : (13.0 * atr4 + tr4) / 14.0

        // D1: rebuild active set (in-episode or within 3% of price), then step
        array.clear(b1Act)
        if b1Count() > 0
            for j = 0 to b1Count() - 1
                if array.get(b1InEp, j) or math.abs(array.get(b1Px, j) - g4C) <= g4C * 0.03
                    array.push(b1Act, j)
        if array.size(b1Act) > 0
            for a = 0 to array.size(b1Act) - 1
                d1Step(array.get(b1Act, a), g4O, g4H, g4L, g4C, pc4, j4)
        // D1 pivot check (candidate = bar B1_S back in the rolling window)
        int rs = array.size(r4H)
        if rs >= 2 * B1_S + 1
            int mp = rs - 1 - B1_S
            float ph = array.get(r4H, mp)
            float wmax = -1e18
            int nmax = 0
            for k = rs - 1 - 2 * B1_S to rs - 1
                float v = array.get(r4H, k)
                wmax := math.max(wmax, v)
                if v == ph
                    nmax += 1
            if ph >= wmax and nmax == 1
                d1Pivot(ph, math.max(array.get(r4O, mp), array.get(r4C, mp)), j4)
            float pl = array.get(r4L, mp)
            float wmin = 1e18
            int nmin = 0
            for k = rs - 1 - 2 * B1_S to rs - 1
                float v = array.get(r4L, k)
                wmin := math.min(wmin, v)
                if v == pl
                    nmin += 1
            if pl <= wmin and nmin == 1
                d1Pivot(pl, math.min(array.get(r4O, mp), array.get(r4C, mp)), j4)

        // D3: body-through decay+count for clusters inside this bar's body
        float blo4 = math.min(g4O, g4C)
        float bhi4 = math.max(g4O, g4C)
        if array.size(c3Sw) > 0
            for k = 0 to array.size(c3Sw) - 1
                if array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
                    float ctr = array.get(c3Swp, k) / array.get(c3Sw, k)
                    if blo4 < ctr and ctr < bhi4
                        float th = array.get(c3Thru, k) * math.pow(2.0, -(day4 - array.get(c3ThruD, k)) / D3_THRUHL)
                        array.set(c3Thru, k, th + 1.0)
                        array.set(c3ThruD, k, day4)
        // D3: body-extreme zigzag -> reversal events
        float thr = D3_ZZ * atr4
        if z3Dir == 0
            if na(z3RunHi) or bhi4 > z3RunHi
                z3RunHi := bhi4
                z3RunHiD := day4
            if na(z3RunLo) or blo4 < z3RunLo
                z3RunLo := blo4
                z3RunLoD := day4
            if not na(atr4) and blo4 <= z3RunHi - thr
                z3PendPx := z3RunHi
                z3PendD := z3RunHiD
                z3PendDir := 1
                z3AmpIn := D3_AMPCAP
                z3Dir := -1
                z3RunPx := blo4
                z3RunD := day4
            else if not na(atr4) and bhi4 >= z3RunLo + thr
                z3PendPx := z3RunLo
                z3PendD := z3RunLoD
                z3PendDir := -1
                z3AmpIn := D3_AMPCAP
                z3Dir := 1
                z3RunPx := bhi4
                z3RunD := day4
        else if z3Dir > 0
            if bhi4 > z3RunPx
                z3RunPx := bhi4
                z3RunD := day4
            if blo4 <= z3RunPx - thr
                float legOut = math.abs(z3RunPx - z3PendPx) / atr4
                d3Add(z3PendPx, z3PendD, z3PendDir, math.sqrt(math.min(math.min(z3AmpIn, legOut), D3_AMPCAP)))
                z3PendPx := z3RunPx
                z3PendD := z3RunD
                z3PendDir := 1
                z3AmpIn := math.min(legOut, D3_AMPCAP)
                z3Dir := -1
                z3RunPx := blo4
                z3RunD := day4
        else
            if blo4 < z3RunPx
                z3RunPx := blo4
                z3RunD := day4
            if bhi4 >= z3RunPx + thr
                float legOut = math.abs(z3PendPx - z3RunPx) / atr4
                d3Add(z3PendPx, z3PendD, z3PendDir, math.sqrt(math.min(math.min(z3AmpIn, legOut), D3_AMPCAP)))
                z3PendPx := z3RunPx
                z3PendD := z3RunD
                z3PendDir := -1
                z3AmpIn := math.min(legOut, D3_AMPCAP)
                z3Dir := 1
                z3RunPx := bhi4
                z3RunD := day4
        prevC4 := g4C
        g4Key := k4
        g4O := open
        g4H := high
        g4L := low
        g4C := close

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Order placement + alerts (orders fill on the signal bar's close; ONE
// consolidated stop+limit exit per entry)
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if strategy.position_size == 0
    inPosB := false

if aLong
    strategy.entry("A-L", strategy.long)
    strategy.exit("A-Lx", "A-L", stop = sigStop, limit = sigLimit)
    lastEntryBar := bar_index
    entryBarIdx  := bar_index
if bLong
    strategy.entry("B-L", strategy.long)
    strategy.exit("B-Lx", "B-L", stop = sigStop, limit = sigLimit)
    lastEntryBar := bar_index
    entryBarIdx  := bar_index
    inPosB := true
if bShort
    strategy.entry("B-S", strategy.short)
    strategy.exit("B-Sx", "B-S", stop = sigStop, limit = sigLimit)
    lastEntryBar := bar_index
    entryBarIdx  := bar_index
    inPosB := true
if cShort
    strategy.entry("C-S", strategy.short)
    strategy.exit("C-Sx", "C-S", stop = sigStop, limit = sigLimit)
    lastEntryBar := bar_index
    entryBarIdx  := bar_index

// B timeout: flat-close a stale momentum position at the bar close
if barstate.isconfirmed and inPosB and strategy.position_size != 0 and bar_index - entryBarIdx >= timeoutB
    strategy.close_all(comment = "B timeout")

// alert() (not alertcondition — inert inside strategies). Create ONE alert on
// this script with condition "Any alert() function call" to receive all.
if aLong
    alert("AutoLevels A: breakout-retest long, level " + str.tostring(aEntryLvl, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if bLong
    alert("AutoLevels B: big-body momentum long", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if bShort
    alert("AutoLevels B: big-body momentum short", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if cShort
    alert("AutoLevels C: rejection short, FVG target", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Drawing — recompute the emitted set on the last bar
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var array<line>  lvLines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label> lvLabels = array.new<label>()

// v6: strategies don't run on the unconfirmed realtime bar, so also draw on
// the last confirmed historical bar — otherwise nothing appears until a bar closes.
if barstate.islast or barstate.islastconfirmedhistory
    if array.size(lvLines) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(lvLines) - 1
            line.delete(array.get(lvLines, j))
    array.clear(lvLines)
    if array.size(lvLabels) > 0
        for j = 0 to array.size(lvLabels) - 1
            label.delete(array.get(lvLabels, j))
    array.clear(lvLabels)

    // ---- D1 emission: gates + score, then greedy min-sep in score order ----
    array<float> d1P = array.new<float>()
    array<float> d1S = array.new<float>()
    if b1Count() > 0
        for j = 0 to b1Count() - 1
            int eps_  = array.get(b1Eps, j)
            int zone_ = array.get(b1Zone, j)
            int ca_   = array.get(b1Ca, j)
            int cb_   = array.get(b1Cb, j)
            bool pass = eps_ >= B1_MINEP and array.get(b1Dep, j) >= B1_MINDEP and
                 zone_ >= B1_ZONEMIN and
                 zone_ / math.max(1, eps_) <= B1_DWELLMX and
                 array.get(b1Bt, j) / math.max(1, zone_) <= B1_BTMAX and
                 math.min(ca_, cb_) >= B1_FLIPMIN and
                 array.get(b1Last, j) - array.get(b1First, j) >= B1_SPANMIN
            if pass
                array.push(d1P, array.get(b1NSmp, j) > 0 ?
                     array.get(b1Sum, j) / array.get(b1NSmp, j) : array.get(b1Px, j))
                array.push(d1S, d1Score(j))
    array<float> d1Out = array.new<float>()
    int n1 = array.size(d1P)
    if n1 > 0
        array<bool> used1 = array.new<bool>(n1, false)
        for it = 0 to n1 - 1
            int bi = -1
            float bs = -1e18
            for q = 0 to n1 - 1
                if not array.get(used1, q) and array.get(d1S, q) > bs
                    bs := array.get(d1S, q)
                    bi := q
            if bi >= 0
                array.set(used1, bi, true)
                float px_ = array.get(d1P, bi)
                bool okSep = true
                if array.size(d1Out) > 0
                    for q = 0 to array.size(d1Out) - 1
                        if math.abs(px_ - array.get(d1Out, q)) <= px_ * B1_MINSEP
                            okSep := false
                if okSep
                    array.push(d1Out, px_)

    // ---- D3 promotion: episode-collapse each cluster, then flip pairs -----
    float today = time / 86400000.0
    array<float> q3P  = array.new<float>()   // candidate price
    array<float> q3S  = array.new<float>()   // candidate score
    array<float> q3Mn = array.new<float>()   // cluster min rep (na for pairs)
    array<float> q3Mx = array.new<float>()
    array<float> q3Hw = array.new<float>()   // decayed hi-rep weight
    array<float> q3Lw = array.new<float>()
    int ncl = array.size(c3Sw)
    int nmm = array.size(m3Cid)
    if ncl > 0 and nmm > 0
        for k = 0 to ncl - 1
            if array.get(c3Sw, k) > 0
                int   nEp = 0
                float prevDay = -1e18
                float epHiW = -1.0
                float epHiPx = na
                float epHiD = na
                float epLoW = -1.0
                float epLoPx = na
                float epLoD = na
                float dw = 0.0
                float minRep = 1e18
                float maxRep = -1e18
                float firstRepD = 1e18
                float lastRepD = -1e18
                float hiW = 0.0
                float loW = 0.0
                for m = 0 to nmm - 1
                    if array.get(m3Cid, m) == k
                        float mday = array.get(m3Day, m)
                        if mday - prevDay >= D3_EPGAP
                            // flush previous episode's representatives
                            if epHiW > 0
                                float wd = epHiW * math.pow(2.0, -(today - epHiD) / D3_HL)
                                dw += wd
                                hiW += wd
                                minRep := math.min(minRep, epHiPx)
                                maxRep := math.max(maxRep, epHiPx)
                                firstRepD := math.min(firstRepD, epHiD)
                                lastRepD := math.max(lastRepD, epHiD)
                            if epLoW > 0
                                float wd = epLoW * math.pow(2.0, -(today - epLoD) / D3_HL)
                                dw += wd
                                loW += wd
                                minRep := math.min(minRep, epLoPx)
                                maxRep := math.max(maxRep, epLoPx)
                                firstRepD := math.min(firstRepD, epLoD)
                                lastRepD := math.max(lastRepD, epLoD)
                            nEp += 1
                            epHiW := -1.0
                            epLoW := -1.0
                        prevDay := mday
                        if array.get(m3Dir, m) > 0
                            if array.get(m3W, m) > epHiW
                                epHiW := array.get(m3W, m)
                                epHiPx := array.get(m3Px, m)
                                epHiD := mday
                        else
                            if array.get(m3W, m) > epLoW
                                epLoW := array.get(m3W, m)
                                epLoPx := array.get(m3Px, m)
                                epLoD := mday
                // flush the final episode
                if epHiW > 0
                    float wd = epHiW * math.pow(2.0, -(today - epHiD) / D3_HL)
                    dw += wd
                    hiW += wd
                    minRep := math.min(minRep, epHiPx)
                    maxRep := math.max(maxRep, epHiPx)
                    firstRepD := math.min(firstRepD, epHiD)
                    lastRepD := math.max(lastRepD, epHiD)
                if epLoW > 0
                    float wd = epLoW * math.pow(2.0, -(today - epLoD) / D3_HL)
                    dw += wd
                    loW += wd
                    minRep := math.min(minRep, epLoPx)
                    maxRep := math.max(maxRep, epLoPx)
                    firstRepD := math.min(firstRepD, epLoD)
                    lastRepD := math.max(lastRepD, epLoD)
                float thruNow = array.get(c3Thru, k) * math.pow(2.0, -(today - array.get(c3ThruD, k)) / D3_THRUHL)
                if nEp >= D3_K and lastRepD - firstRepD >= D3_SPAN and dw >= D3_WMIN and
                     thruNow / math.max(1, nEp) <= D3_THRUMAX
                    array.push(q3P, (minRep + maxRep) / 2.0)
                    array.push(q3S, dw)
                    array.push(q3Mn, minRep)
                    array.push(q3Mx, maxRep)
                    array.push(q3Hw, hiW)
                    array.push(q3Lw, loW)
    // flip-pair candidates from price-adjacent promoted clusters
    int n3 = array.size(q3P)
    if n3 > 1
        array<int> ord3 = array.new<int>()
        array<bool> used3 = array.new<bool>(n3, false)
        for it = 0 to n3 - 1
            int bi = -1
            float bp = 1e18
            for q = 0 to n3 - 1
                if not array.get(used3, q) and array.get(q3P, q) < bp
                    bp := array.get(q3P, q)
                    bi := q
            if bi >= 0
                array.set(used3, bi, true)
                array.push(ord3, bi)
        for a = 0 to array.size(ord3) - 2
            int lo_ = array.get(ord3, a)
            int hi_ = array.get(ord3, a + 1)
            float gapPx = array.get(q3Mn, hi_) - array.get(q3Mx, lo_)
            if gapPx > 0 and gapPx <= D3_PAIRGAP * array.get(q3Mx, lo_) and
                 array.get(q3Hw, lo_) > 0 and array.get(q3Lw, hi_) > 0
                array.push(q3P, (array.get(q3Mx, lo_) + array.get(q3Mn, hi_)) / 2.0)
                array.push(q3S, D3_PAIRBST * (array.get(q3Hw, lo_) + array.get(q3Lw, hi_)))
                array.push(q3Mn, float(na))
                array.push(q3Mx, float(na))
                array.push(q3Hw, 0.0)
                array.push(q3Lw, 0.0)
    // greedy keep: desc score, min-sep 0.20%, <= 2 kept per ±0.60%
    array<float> d3Out = array.new<float>()
    int n3b = array.size(q3P)
    if n3b > 0
        array<bool> used3b = array.new<bool>(n3b, false)
        for it = 0 to n3b - 1
            int bi = -1
            float bs = -1e18
            for q = 0 to n3b - 1
                if not array.get(used3b, q) and array.get(q3S, q) > bs
                    bs := array.get(q3S, q)
                    bi := q
            if bi >= 0
                array.set(used3b, bi, true)
                float px_ = array.get(q3P, bi)
                bool okSep = true
                int nNear = 0
                if array.size(d3Out) > 0
                    for q = 0 to array.size(d3Out) - 1
                        float kp = array.get(d3Out, q)
                        if math.abs(px_ - kp) <= px_ * D3_MINSEP
                            okSep := false
                        if math.abs(px_ - kp) <= px_ * 0.0060
                            nNear += 1
                if okSep and nNear < D3_CAPM
                    array.push(d3Out, px_)

    // ---- SYNTHESIS: pool D1+D3, mean-linkage cluster, rank, cap ----------
    array<float> pP = array.new<float>()
    array<int>  pSrc = array.new<int>()
    if array.size(d1Out) > 0
        for q = 0 to array.size(d1Out) - 1
            array.push(pP, array.get(d1Out, q))
            array.push(pSrc, 1)
    if array.size(d3Out) > 0
        for q = 0 to array.size(d3Out) - 1
            array.push(pP, array.get(d3Out, q))
            array.push(pSrc, 3)
    // sort pool ascending (selection)
    int np = array.size(pP)
    array<float> cP = array.new<float>()     // cluster placement
    array<int>  cT = array.new<int>()        // tier: 2 = both detectors
    if np > 0
        array<bool> usedP = array.new<bool>(np, false)
        float cSum = 0.0
        int   cN = 0
        bool  c1 = false
        bool  c3f = false
        for it = 0 to np - 1
            int bi = -1
            float bp = 1e18
            for q = 0 to np - 1
                if not array.get(usedP, q) and array.get(pP, q) < bp
                    bp := array.get(pP, q)
                    bi := q
            if bi >= 0
                array.set(usedP, bi, true)
                float px_ = array.get(pP, bi)
                if cN > 0 and px_ - cSum / cN <= SYN_TOL * px_
                    cSum += px_
                    cN += 1
                    if array.get(pSrc, bi) == 1
                        c1 := true
                    else
                        c3f := true
                else
                    if cN > 0
                        array.push(cP, cSum / cN)
                        array.push(cT, c1 and c3f ? 2 : 1)
                    cSum := px_
                    cN := 1
                    c1 := array.get(pSrc, bi) == 1
                    c3f := array.get(pSrc, bi) == 3
        if cN > 0
            array.push(cP, cSum / cN)
            array.push(cT, c1 and c3f ? 2 : 1)
    // trailing 60-day range
    float rlo = na
    float rhi = na
    int nd = array.size(dKey)
    if nd > 0
        for q = math.max(0, nd - SYN_RANGED) to nd - 1
            rlo := na(rlo) ? array.get(dLo, q) : math.min(rlo, array.get(dLo, q))
            rhi := na(rhi) ? array.get(dHi, q) : math.max(rhi, array.get(dHi, q))
    // greedy emission: tier-2 first (ascending), then singletons desc price
    array<float> synP = array.new<float>()
    array<int>  synT = array.new<int>()
    int inRange = 0
    int ncc = array.size(cP)
    if ncc > 0
        for pass_ = 2 to 1
            for step_ = 0 to ncc - 1
                int q = pass_ == 2 ? step_ : ncc - 1 - step_
                if array.get(cT, q) == pass_
                    float px_ = array.get(cP, q)
                    bool okSep = true
                    if array.size(synP) > 0
                        for w = 0 to array.size(synP) - 1
                            if math.abs(px_ - array.get(synP, w)) <= px_ * SYN_MINSEP
                                okSep := false
                    bool inR = not na(rlo) and px_ >= rlo and px_ <= rhi
                    if okSep and (not inR or inRange < SYN_CAP)
                        array.push(synP, px_)
                        array.push(synT, array.get(cT, q))
                        if inR
                            inRange += 1

    // ---- draw the boundary levels ----------------------------------------
    if array.size(synP) > 0
        for q = 0 to array.size(synP) - 1
            float px_ = array.get(synP, q)
            color col = px_ > close ? resColor : supColor
            bool  two = array.get(synT, q) == 2
            array.push(lvLines, line.new(bar_index, px_, bar_index + 1, px_,
                 extend = extend.both, color = col, width = two ? 2 : 1))
            if showLabels
                string txt = str.tostring(px_, format.mintick) + (two ? " ●●" : "")
                array.push(lvLabels, label.new(bar_index + 2, px_, txt,
                     style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(col, 82),
                     textcolor = col, size = size.small))
    int nBoundary = array.size(synP)

    // Status table — first thing to check when the chart looks empty.
    if showStats
        var table st = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 5,
             bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 88), border_width = 1,
             border_color = color.new(color.gray, 70))
        table.cell(st, 0, 0, "Bars loaded",     text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 1, 0, str.tostring(bar_index + 1),        text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 0, 1, "4h bars built",   text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 1, 1, str.tostring(j4 + 1),               text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 0, 2, "Boundary lines",  text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 1, 2, str.tostring(nBoundary),            text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 0, 3, "Trading book",    text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 1, 3, str.tostring(levelCount()),         text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        string hint = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) > 14400 ?
             "chart TF coarser than 4h — use 15m, 1h or 4h" :
             nBoundary == 0 ? (j4 < 90 ? "warming up — boundaries need weeks of 4h history" :
                  "no boundary passed the gates yet — load more history") :
             timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) > 3600 ?
                  "lines OK · trading layer validated on 15m" : "OK"
        table.cell(st, 0, 4, "Status",          text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
        table.cell(st, 1, 4, hint,                               text_size = size.small, text_color = chart.fg_color)
